The attached champions.png shows the REAL champion portraits of our game Backyard Monsters Revamped (Gorgo the blue ape, Drull the red two-headed dragon, Fomor the purple winged beast, Korath the lava beast, Krallen the leopard beast), each at level 1, 3 and 6 in its two looks. Study the painting style, polish, lighting (soft key light from the upper left, soft shadow on the ground) and above all HOW A CHAMPION GROWS: level 1 is a small chubby baby, level 3 is the grown creature, level 6 is the same creature bigger and older wearing battle armour (straps, plates, metal spikes) bolted to its body. It is ONE design that grows, never separate designs.

Job: design a NEW champion for a Christmas-only "Frost Tribe" of wild monsters. It must be a brand-new creature, not a recolour of any champion in champions.png, and it must NOT look like an ape or gorilla (Gorgo is a blue ape). Frost tribe mark: glowing pale icy-cyan eyes, frost, snow on top surfaces, translucent pale-blue ice crystal for spikes and horns. Painted at the same detail and quality as the reference champions; no outline; no text; no Santa hats or costume items.

The creature: "GLACIER BEHEMOTH", a heavy ground tank. A massive, low, broad four-legged beast like a cross between a tortoise and a rhino, thick elephant-like legs, a short heavy head with a wide jaw of blunt tusks and a single thick ice horn on its nose. Its back is a frozen shell: a slab of glacier ice with crystal spires growing out of it. Hide: cold slate-blue-grey, rough and pebbled, with white frost; belly paler.
- Level 1: a small round baby, stubby legs, a tiny smooth ice nub on its nose, just a few little crystal points on a soft rounded back, big icy eyes.
- Level 3: the full beast, the ice-shell back with a cluster of tall crystal spires, the nose horn grown, tusks out.
- Level 6: the same beast bigger and older, the spires taller and more numerous like a small glacier ridge, and battle armour: dark iron plates strapped over the shoulders and head with riveted metal bands and iron-capped tusks, chains of icicles hanging from the plates.

Canvas 1536x1024 split into 2 columns x 2 rows of equal cells (768x512 each). Each cell has the creature on the same plain light grey-beige studio ground as the game's monster portraits, with a soft shadow, all seen from the same front-left camera about 30 degrees above. Keep ONE scale for all three levels, so the creature visibly grows: level 1 about 35% of the cell height, level 3 about 65%, level 6 about 90%.
- Row 1, column 1: LEVEL 1.
- Row 1, column 2: LEVEL 3.
- Row 2, column 1: LEVEL 6.
- Row 2, column 2: the LEVEL 3 creature in action, using its power: it stamps a front foot and a ring of jagged ice shards bursts from the ground in front of it, frost spreading over the ground.
No grid lines, no numbers, no text, no labels, no frame.
Save the final PNG as champ-glacier.png in the current working directory.

